        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by improper handling of the case where the XML header was not found. The original code attempted to read the header without first checking if it existed, leading to potential null pointer dereferences and resource leaks when the header was absent. This oversight resulted in the failure to clean up allocated resources properly, which could lead to memory issues.

        Commit message:
        fixing bad resource cleanup in ismrmrd_read_header

